================================================================================================
 (D) THE ι-ODD INDEX = the quadratic GAUSS SUM g_p (Borsuk-Ulam odd degree)
================================================================================================
  p=7: χ(-1)=(-1|7)=-1  => χ is ODD (p=3 mod4, -1 non-residue => FREE ι)
  Gauss sum g_7 = Σ_a (a|7) e(a/7) = +0.000000+2.645751j
    |g|=2.645751 vs sqrt(7)=2.645751; g = i*sqrt(p)? True
  => g_7 = i*sqrt(7): a SINGLE nonzero ι-ODD trace. Being nonzero, Borsuk-Ulam CERTIFIES a lonely runner
     (the odd/reduced index obstructs an ι-equivariant cover). This is the certification, not Λ(ι)=0.

================================================================================================
 THE BYPASS (framing)
================================================================================================
 Naive: L = Σ_A (-1)^|A| I_A is absolutely DIVERGENT (Σ|c_k|~; MISTAKE-078) -- signed cancellation opaque.
 Lefschetz split: L = (ι-EVEN main term, the (6/7)^13 average, positive) + (ι-ODD correction).
  * ι acts FREELY => ordinary Lefschetz Λ(ι)=0 (no ι-fixed lonely pt): the EVEN index cannot see it.
  * The ι-ODD index localizes to the quadratic character => the GAUSS SUM g_7=i*sqrt(7) (ONE number),
    computed by the three pillars (Borsuk-Ulam odd degree / i*sqrt(7) / the p=7 apex).
 => Replace the divergent series by the single Gauss-sum trace: the odd index certifies M>=1/n WITHOUT
    summing the signed correction. This is why p=3mod4 needs Borsuk-Ulam (odd/Gauss) not Brouwer (even).
